{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "A small country on Roshar beside Alethkar, long the traditional first target of Alethi conquest.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "52" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "A country on Roshar whose tight-knit people, the Herdazians, are spread across the east, many living in Alethkar and Jah Keved.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-4" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" },
            { "book": "lost-metal", "chapter": "32" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "Herdazian families are huge, so a single person may be kin to half the country, and Herdazians stand by one another wherever they live. Across western Roshar they are thought extremely boastful, and their women tough and hard to impress.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-4" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fromCulture": "people"
    },
    {
      "text": "Herdazian cooking relies on many kinds of shellfood and on flatbread, and chull head counts as a delicacy. The best-known dish is chouta: Soulcast meat, fried, rolled tight in flatbread and topped with sauce.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "46" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "13" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fromCulture": "food"
    },
    {
      "text": "Herdazian fingernails are crystalline and slate-coloured, hard enough to strike a fire with.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "26" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "43" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "35" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fromCulture": "people"
    },
    {
      "text": "Herdaz is a kingdom whose king comes from a fairly new dynasty.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "49" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Herdazian Vorinism allows men to read.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "12" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "50" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fromCulture": "religion"
    },
    {
      "text": "The crown owns one Shardblade and one set of Shardplate, which pass down the royal line.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "23" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "75" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Most of the country is a run of long, narrow peninsulas reaching into the sea. The interior is fairly flat, divided by one major river.",
      "revealedIn": ["oathbringer"]
    }
  ],
