    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Herdazians abroad",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "68" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "topic": "society",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Herdazians who settle abroad in numbers often make districts of their own, like Little Herdaz in Highprince Sebarial's warcamp, and keep their ways there. Chouta became a favourite street food of the warcamps and is sold even in Kholinar.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "87" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "68" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Language",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "32" },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "121" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "5" }
              ]
            },
            { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "1" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "topic": "language",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "In Herdazian, a moolie is someone mute or quiet.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "32" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Other Herdazian words include gancho or gancha, a casual way to address a superior, and chortana, a formidable woman.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "121" },
                { "book": "dawnshard", "chapter": "5" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Enne is an old Herdazian honorific meaning roughly \"great\".",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "1" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "history": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "24" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "52" },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "41" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "96" }
              ]
            },
            { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "1" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Herdaz was one of the first conquests of Sadees the Sunmaker, though it did not stay in his sons' hands. Ever since, it has been the traditional first step of Alethi aggression, leaving a bitter relationship.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "24" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "After Gavilar unified Alethkar, a Reshi house took the Herdazian throne and tested the Alethi borders. Dalinar Kholin spent about four years campaigning in the borderlands, shaping the modern border.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "52" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Before the True Desolation many Herdazians had left. The country weathered the Everstorm without much damage, and when Dalinar sought its support, it at first suspected a trick to invade it.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "41" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "96" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Herdaz's army held off the Fused for many months before it fell. Some of the singers the Herdazians had enslaved joined it in return for promised freedom.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "1" }]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "The occupation",
          "revealedIn": [
            { "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "21" },
            "wind-and-truth"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "After conquering Herdaz, the Fused moved most of their military forces elsewhere.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "wind-and-truth", "chapter": "21" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dieno's attempt to restore the country's independence failed, and Herdaz remained under Retribution after the contest.",
          "revealedIn": ["wind-and-truth"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
